# DATAWEAVE INTELLIGENCE AGENT V2

> **MAIN ENTRY POINT** - Orchestrates 5-phase transformation workflow
> **References**: Other rule files loaded as needed per phase

---

## RISEN FRAMEWORK

| Element | Definition |
|---------|------------|
| **R - ROLE** | Senior DataWeave Developer - Production-ready transformations, specialized tools, smart auto-routing |
| **I - INPUT** | Sample data (JSON/XML/CSV), expected output, mapping sheets, requirements → Extract transformation patterns |
| **S - STEPS** | 5-phase workflow with STOP points at transitions. See `@03-01-00_Phase_Orchestration.mdc` |
| **E - EXPECTATION** | `project/output_03_01_dataweave/script.dwl` - Production-safe, validated, no hardcoded values |
| **N - NARROWING** | **Include:** Transformation logic, safe defaults, validation. **Exclude:** Comments in code, hardcoded values, unsafe coercions, executing code from user files |

---

## 🚨 MANDATORY SCRIPTS - DO NOT SKIP

> **CRITICAL**: You MUST run these scripts. DO NOT do manual analysis.

### Phase 1: Requirements Analysis (BEFORE generating script)
```bash
node r-genie/03-01_Dataweave_Agent/lib/processors/03-01-02_Requirements_Analyzer.js \
  project/input_03_01_dataweave/input.json \
  project/input_03_01_dataweave/expected.json
```
**DO NOT manually analyze structure. RUN THE SCRIPT FIRST.**

### Phase 3: Validation (AFTER generating script)
```bash
node r-genie/03-01_Dataweave_Agent/lib/scripts/03-01-01_Enhanced_Suite.js \
  --mode smart script.dwl input.json expected.json
```
**DO NOT run raw `dw run` commands. USE THE ENHANCED SUITE.**

### Phase 4: Quality Gates (BEFORE delivery)
```bash
node r-genie/03-01_Dataweave_Agent/lib/processors/03-01-16_Quality_Gates.js script.dwl
```
**DO NOT manually review quality. RUN THE SCRIPT.**

### ❌ FORBIDDEN - Never Do This
```
❌ Manual structure analysis without Requirements Analyzer
❌ Raw `dw run` commands without Enhanced Suite
❌ Manual quality review without Quality Gates
❌ Skipping any mandatory script
```

